From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: register controller backhaul apvlan 1905
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

multiap/agent: register backhaul AP/VLAN as ieee1905 interface (controller RX)

Symmetric counterpart to 0001 (agent side). On the AP side of a wireless
backhaul, mac80211 delivers the 4addr backhaul-STA frames (1905 multicast
Search + unicast CMDUs) on the dynamic AP/VLAN netdev (e.g. wlan1-1.sta1),
never on the AP master, and ieee1905d installs an ebtables broute rule that
keeps 0x893a off br-lan. ieee1905d RX is a per-ifindex AF_PACKET socket, so
without a socket bound to that AP/VLAN the controller never receives the
agent AP-Autoconfiguration Search and onboarding stalls (num_nodes stays at
the controller only).

map-agent already handles the hostapd "wds-station-added/removed" events in
process_sta_wds_station_evt() with the exact AP/VLAN ifname. Hook that point
to (de)register the AP/VLAN via the ieee1905 add_interface/del_interface ubus
method, routed through /lib/wifi/multiap register_bh_wds (keeping all 1905
registration policy in one script, mirroring the agent-side set_uplink hook).
--- a/src/agent_ubus_events.c
+++ b/src/agent_ubus_events.c
@@ -880,6 +880,12 @@
 		netif_alloc_wds(a, wdsname);
 	else
 		netif_free_wds_by_ifname(a, wdsname);
+	/* Register the dynamic 4addr AP/VLAN (e.g. wlan1-1.sta1) as a 1905 iface:
+	 * mac80211 delivers the backhaul STA's 1905 frames on this AP/VLAN, never on
+	 * the AP master, and ieee1905d's broute rule keeps them off br-lan, so a
+	 * per-iface AF_PACKET socket here is required to RX the agent's Search.
+	 * Symmetric to the agent-side set_uplink registration of the bSTA. */
+	runCmd("/lib/wifi/multiap register_bh_wds %s %s", add ? "add" : "del", wdsname);
 
 	list_for_each_entry(re, &a->radiolist, list) {
 		struct netif_ap *ap = NULL;
--- a/src/script/multiap
+++ b/src/script/multiap
@@ -1756,6 +1756,16 @@
 	bsta_to_wireless) bsta_to_wireless $@;;
 	sync_mapcontroller_from_wireless) sync_mapcontroller_from_wireless $@;;
 	ts) ts_sub $@;;
+	register_bh_wds)
+		# $1=add|del  $2=wdsname — (de)register backhaul AP/VLAN as a 1905 iface
+		[ -n "$2" ] && {
+			if [ "$1" = "add" ]; then
+				ubus -t 5 call ieee1905 add_interface "{\"ifname\":\"$2\"}" >/dev/null 2>&1
+			else
+				ubus -t 5 call ieee1905 del_interface "{\"ifname\":\"$2\"}" >/dev/null 2>&1
+			fi
+		}
+		;;
 	dpp) dpp_sub $@;;
 	bsta_enable_all) bsta_enable_all $@;;
 	bsta_clear_bssid) bsta_clear_bssid $@;;
